Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 08:34:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] A re-pin is its own PR, holding only pins
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Owner ruling, 2026-11-07 (about 08:28Z): "Keep repins on own PR so easier
to stack dependencies".

- remote-mount §"Re-pinning": a re-pin PR changes the pins and what
  regenerates from them, nothing else; features that need the new pins
  stack on it; a fix the re-pin needs lands in its owning layer. Counter-
  example: folio-assistant#2985 carried #2999 and a caches:viz gate line.
- index-config: the same, in its re-pin paragraph.
- merge-manager-watcher sweep rule 10: a re-pin PR carrying other changes
  is sent back to be split onto a stacked PR or into the owning layer.
- continual-progress, coordinate: the sibling's side.
- merge-request.bpmn: the stacking step says so; .pot regenerated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VQDpPc2tT1vUufdyDbQTBz
